## How to ingest a new source

When a new file appears in `raw-sources/` (or the user says "I just added X, ingest it"):

1. Read the file completely. Do not skim.
2. Identify what kind of source it is: SOP, framework, transcript, ICP doc, script, content idea, client material, or inspiration.
3. Tell the user the 5â€“10 most important takeaways before writing anything. Wait for direction if the source is large or the user wants to guide emphasis.
4. Write a summary page in the appropriate `wiki/` subfolder. Filename is kebab-case, descriptive, scannable: `profile-funnel-mechanics.md`, not `summary-2026-04.md`.
5. Update `index.md` â€” add a new entry with link, one-line summary, category, date.
6. Update every existing wiki page the new source touches. A single SOP can update 10â€“15 pages: concept pages get new examples, playbooks get new steps, the Marcus page gets new pain points, the glossary gets new terms.
